  "result": "**Short answer:** The repo has no amount-based approval rule that is in force. Current code allows any Approver or Admin to approve any amount with one approval.\n\n- **Who can approve (in code):** `ApprovalsController.cs:9` has `[RequireRole(\"Approver\", \"Admin\")]`, so a 75,000 invoice can be approved by either role, with one approval. `ApprovalService.Approve` has no amount check.\n- **600,000 invoice:** The only amount rule is in the brief `docs/use-cases/UC-1-bulk-approval.md:17`: \"Invoices over $1,000 need a second approver before they are final.\" That is a proposed feature, not implemented. Under that brief, a 600,000 invoice needs **two approvals**. The brief does not name the roles for the second approver, and its open questions (line 26) ask whether one person can be both approvers.",
